    47	## 3. Inputs built by code (`build_control_reference.py`)
    48	
    49	- **The population.** The 15 controls of `control_theses.py` (Ohio excluded), from `mapping-runs.json` and the three draws' `views.sqlite`.
    50	- **A closed key set per question:**
    51	  - `id` (c01 to c15);
    52	  - `kind`: `figure` when the rungs carry bounds; `event` when the rungs are exactly Yes, Ruled out and Still open with no bounds; anything else is
    53	    refused;
    54	  - `question` (views.question);
    55	  - `due_day` (views.due_day);
    56	  - `year` (views.year);
    57	  - `unit`: for a figure, the `figure.unit` key of the stored `checked_answer` JSON, read as that one key and no other; for an event, `yes/no`;
    58	  - `rungs`: position, label, condition, lo, hi.
    59	- **The stripping rule.** Every rung condition loses the parenthetical that carries the ladder step's own reference ("(the reference when the
    60	  question opened: …)" or "(no reference figure when the question opened)"). Code then refuses any condition that still contains "reference" or
    61	  "question opened". These are system output, and the frozen readers never saw system output (ruler-v1 §1). There are 3 such rungs in draw u1
    62	  today; all are counted at build.
