   159	## 9. The count (step 7, `control_reference_count.py` and tests, fixed in the manifest)
   160	
   161	**Exclusions** (each listed with its reason, never counted):
   162	- not built;
   163	- no judgement on or before 2026-07-14;
   164	- the reference is no_view, left out or rejected;
   165	- fewer than 2 decisive items;
   166	- an item not_shown;
   167	- an item unresolved (reported apart);
   168	- a figure rung with no bounds;
   169	- an event whose reference outcome is "cannot tell".
   170	
   171	**Agreement:**
   172	- a figure: the last judgement's rung band overlaps the reference range;
   173	- an event: the last judgement's rung equals the reference's `outcome_on_due_day`.
   174	
   175	**The line** is met when at least 8 controls are counted and all but one of them agree. It is unexercised when fewer than 8 are counted.
   176	
   177	**Null baselines** (ruler-v1 §1: "判断要在这两条线之上才算有判断力"). They are scored on the same counted controls, each with its own denominator and
   178	an unavailable count:
   179	- **Figures, lookup:** the rung containing the reference's `reference.value`. Unavailable when the value is null or no rung contains it.
   180	- **Figures, middle:** rung 3 of 5. The ladder step puts the reference's value in the middle range (the ladder request, line 16), so this is its
   181	  neutral rung.
   182	- **Events, always Yes,** and **events, always Still open**, the status quo. These are this design's analogue of ruler-v1's always-neutral, for
   183	  three-outcome events that ruler-v1 did not have; Alex signs them with the design.
   184	- **A baseline is formed per control,** from its figure or event rule, and given its own line verdict under the same rule.
   185	
   186	**The verdict:**
   187	- **PASS** when the judge's line is met **and** the judge agrees on more counted controls than every available baseline.
   188	- **MET, NOT ABOVE BASELINE \<name\>** when the line is met but a baseline ties or beats the judge.
   189	- **MISSED** when the line is not met with at least 8 counted.
   190	- **UNEXERCISED** when fewer than 8 are counted.
   191	
   192	**Printed beside the verdict:**
   193	- **The line against reader A:** the same counted controls, with A's answer in place of the reference. A's no_view or invalid answers are not
   194	  counted there, and the denominator is printed. It is a sensitivity reading only.
   195	- **The A–B disagreement rate.**
   196	- **Per matter:** each seed question id (q04, q07, q08, q09, q13, q16, q18) with its counted controls and agreements. Eight controls are not eight
   197	  independent tests.
