   240	| Strip the ladder's reference from the rungs | ruler-v1 §1 (readers see no system output) |
   241	| Freeze and correction records | ruler-v1 §2; D261 |
   242	
   243	## 13. What it does not measure, and its weak points
   244	
   245	- **Not measured:** whether the right questions were opened (D1); delivery beyond the shown filter (D2); the judge's daily path.
   246	- **Model-authored.** Alex's signature is the human vote, and the noise is printed.
   247	- **One stored run, on the luna configuration's questions:**
   248	  - PASS shows the line exercised and met on these 15. It does not pass Stage B, which also missed the strictest last-answer reading.
   249	  - MISSED is a finding about the judge or the reference on these questions, and stops the line before further spend (D355).
   250	  - UNEXERCISED names its causes.
   251	- **Tuning exposure.** If a miss leads to a judge change (D263), these 15 become tuning data, and the next application must be on unseen
   252	  questions.
   253	
   254	## 14. Changes from version 2
   255	
   256	- **Ohio dropped:** 15 questions, as Alex's option says.
   257	- **Option text recorded word for word.** The material now has stronger sources.
   258	- **Readers work inline** with no tool access, both families' logs are checked, and A follows the frozen runner's precedent.
   259	- **The ladder's reference is stripped from the rungs** by a stated rule.
   260	- **Kind and unit derivation stated.** A build refusal stops the whole build.
   261	- **Every participant-facing text and the scorer** are fixed by sha before step 2 (§0).
   262	- **Events** are compared by the reference's `outcome_on_due_day`, with "cannot tell" excluded.
   263	- **Baselines defined,** each with its own verdict; PASS requires the judge to beat them.
   264	- **The line against A** has its population and denominator stated.
   265	- **Signing:** Alex's alone; the closed set gains "leave out" and "reject"; no recommendation on disputed questions; the line waits while he is
   266	  inactive.
   267	- **The items-only brief** is fixed in the manifest. Its third readers rule without the answers; "unresolved" is reported apart from "not_shown".
   268	- **Validity schema closed.** Failure states are complete (§11). Sources are listed (§12).

