**Version 3 is not ready.** It fixes the main event-comparison problem, but its new pass rule changes the agreed control line and can compare counts from different populations. It also leaves the reference-building schema and input checks incomplete.

For example, if the judge agrees on 7 of 8 controls and a baseline is available on only 2, comparing **7** with **2** would call the judge better without comparing either answer on the same two questions.

1. **Event comparison.** `outcome_on_due_day` addresses the round-2 defect: “Ruled out” and “Still open” are now separate, and “cannot tell” is excluded. That is consistent with the distinction Alex chose for event outcomes. The implementation still needs to say that the stored judgment’s **rung position must be resolved to its label and condition** before comparison; the stored value is an index, while the reference field is text. The validity rule also says “Yes exactly when `yes_no` is true,” but does not explain whether `cannot tell` can coexist with an uncertain yes/no answer. [Design](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/stage-b-controls/NEW-REFERENCE-DESIGN-v3.md:86), [D409](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:4502), [stored comparison](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/stage_b/control_theses.py:101).

2. **Signing.** The closed set now includes Alex’s own validated answer, no-view and rejection, and signing waits for him. That closes most of the earlier gap. It must also state that A, B and third-reader answers offered for selection must themselves be valid; an invalid row cannot become valid merely because Alex selects it. Define how the reason and status of an unresolved row are recorded if he rejects it. [Design](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/stage-b-controls/NEW-REFERENCE-DESIGN-v3.md:120).

3. **Access boundary.** Inline prompts, disallowed tools and checks for both families are stronger. The closed question fields also distinguish showing all choices from revealing the selected one. But the input manifest omits the three `archive.sqlite` files, even though the shown-material check reads judge requests from them. A changed archive could therefore change that check without tripping the stated manifest. Include the archives and the run record that selects the completed attempt, or freeze and hash an equivalent extracted input before readers run. [Design](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/stage-b-controls/NEW-REFERENCE-DESIGN-v3.md:66), [request collection](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/stage_b/control_theses.py:65), [run selection](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/stage_b/stored_judgements.py:61).

   The statement that nothing participants see is written after the first reader runs is also too broad: reconciliation, retries and the signing page necessarily contain later answers. The useful rule is to freeze their **generators, templates, permitted inputs and checks** beforehand, then retain the generated outputs and hashes. [Design](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/stage-b-controls/NEW-REFERENCE-DESIGN-v3.md:14).

4. **Failure states.** Whole-build refusal, retries, third-reader failures, Alex’s absence and shown-check splits now have outcomes. Still specify resumption after interruption, incomplete or failed log inspection, a missing signing choice, and what happens when the signed reference or shown-check output fails its hash or shape check. These should stop scoring, rather than be treated as ordinary excluded controls. [State table](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/stage-b-controls/NEW-REFERENCE-DESIGN-v3.md:209).

5. **Other round-2 findings.**

   - **Items-only brief:** the relevant same-fact rule and blind third-reader procedure are specified, and unresolved is separated from not shown. The actual brief is not yet available for review. The design also discloses the remaining timing limit: an item seen after the final judgment does not prove that judgment saw it. [Design](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/stage-b-controls/NEW-REFERENCE-DESIGN-v3.md:146).
   - **Validity:** improved, but “the brief’s keys, with the types the brief gives” is not a closed schema. Define exact allowed keys and types, including nested item lists, booleans, finite numbers, direction consistency and the shape of `no_view`. The reconciliation rule also omits **both readers saying `no_view`**. The two-item minimum is sourced to the frozen definition, but the procedure should report a reader unable to cite two items as unresolved rather than induce an unsupported citation. [Design](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/stage-b-controls/NEW-REFERENCE-DESIGN-v3.md:91), [frozen brief](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/judgement-gold/reader-brief.md:26).
   - **Baselines:** availability and denominators are partly specified, but the verdict compares raw agreement counts even when denominators differ. Compare judge and baseline on the **same controls**, print both counts and the unavailable cases, and specify the outcome when a baseline is unavailable for every control. [Design](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/stage-b-controls/NEW-REFERENCE-DESIGN-v3.md:177).
   - **Against A:** the same starting population and A’s exclusions are now stated. Also specify that an A event answer of `cannot tell` is unavailable, and label this a sensitivity reading because material shown was checked against the signed reference’s items, not necessarily A’s. [Design](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/stage-b-controls/NEW-REFERENCE-DESIGN-v3.md:192).
   - **Predictions:** the old eight is correctly labelled a historical count, and an unexercised result is no longer attributed automatically to delivery. [Design](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/stage-b-controls/NEW-REFERENCE-DESIGN-v3.md:199).

